Package: iommu-map-pa-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dkms
Conflicts: upcie-iommu-map-dkms
Replaces: upcie-iommu-map-dkms
Description: experimental helper mapping physical addresses into an IOMMU domain (DKMS)
 Standalone out-of-tree kernel module serving the IOMMU_MAP_PA /
 IOMMU_UNMAP_PA ioctls on a dedicated /dev/iommu_map_pa misc device. Given a
 PCI BDF, an array of physical addresses (e.g. a dma-buf-derived phys_lut for
 GPU memory), and a userspace-chosen IOVA base, it installs the addresses into
 the IOMMU domain the device currently uses. For a VFIO-controlled NVMe this
 makes GPU memory reachable for P2P DMA: userspace builds NVMe PRPs from the
 IOVA range.
 .
 The module is an experimental proof of concept. It borrows a live IOMMU
 domain it does not own and bypasses VFIO and iommufd IOVA accounting; see
 the README for the strict mapping and lifetime requirements. The target must
 already be in a userspace-owned domain, and the device node is root-only,
 because mapping arbitrary physical addresses for a DMA-capable device is
 equivalent to raw physical memory access. Built and installed via DKMS, it
 rebuilds automatically on kernel updates with no custom kernel required.
